what to do for the workaround","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1553514794,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3NjE2NDE3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3206#issuecomment-476164178"},"message":"[ The install command fails on my end, so I haven't tried to run it but... ]\n\nWhile not unlocking outputs would allow you to work around this issue, it looks like a bug in `_unlock_or_remove`s logic: it doesn't consider that the path could be a directory.\n\nSo an immediate workaround would (hopefully) be to (1) explicitly list the output paths or (2) drop --output and let the automatic output detection happen on the initial run.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1558718146,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5NTcxNTg1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3206#issuecomment-495715859"},"message":"keep running into it... just need to not use `run` in the short run ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1563993466,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUxNDc1MDI0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3206#issuecomment-514750242"},"message":"and again.  I have ~1400 .feat directories already, need to produce more for the missing ones (~300 more), so need to run something like\n\n```shell\nfor f in *.fsf; do ff=${f/.fsf/.feat}; [ -e $ff ] || echo $f; done| xargs parallel -j 2  ../../.datalad/environments/fslanal/run feat -- \n```\n\nAs output I want to just say `--output '*.feat'` since have no time (and might exhaust command line max size) to get those 400 `--output` entries.  But I cannot wait for the outputs to get unlocked.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1565145873,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUxODkxNzA4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3206#issuecomment-518917082"},"message":"The \"unlock\" stage disabling would be also handy for `rerun`.  ATM `rerun` unlocks all outputs as found in the initial `run`.  But I often rerun some elder commit to just \"add\" more results based on new files added to the dataset (so my initial command checks first either results are available already like in the example above). So unlocking of prior outputs is really not necessary and just wastes time.  Disabling unlocking could also be taken as additional measure to prevent some incorrect execution (since command would fail it decides to write to some files which it was not supposed to).","files":null}]}